learnings[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-13T22:07:15.884Z","harness:codex","A migration flag can belong to a universal output dimension without being replaceable by the universal option. Promise strength must be explicit contract data: parsing a well-formed hint or checking that its target flag exists cannot distinguish projection equivalence from preserved traversal, grouping, side-effect, cursor, or streaming semantics."
  "2026-08-15T18:45:11.542Z","harness:codex",Stable recursive obligation identifiers must encode each path segment before concatenation. Delimiter joining raw producer keys is not injective and can let one proof discharge a structurally different reference.
  "2026-08-16T19:27:30.614Z","harness:codex","A source census proves vocabulary coverage and detects untyped producer drift, but it is not execution evidence; keep producer discovery separate from per-value reachability and semantic-equivalence proof."
  "2026-08-19T05:28:39.600Z","harness:codex","Per-kind runtime coverage closes vocabulary blind spots but is not equivalent to per-producer execution. Keep source population, distinct emitted values, and executable obligations separate in receipts so a small runtime sample cannot masquerade as exhaustive producer coverage."
  "2026-08-19T07:42:40.620Z","harness:codex","A public contract-only entrypoint should depend on declarative vocabularies, not runtime query implementations. Separate projection constants and validators into a dependency-light module, then re-export them from legacy entrypoints to preserve compatibility while keeping contract import costs bounded."
  "2026-08-19T18:27:47.015Z","harness:codex",Linked test commands are durable PM contracts and must be migrated alongside test file organization; a passing source suite does not excuse a stale executable evidence path.
